<===> README.md
Like dart-sass, quoted strings in raw CSS contexts (custom properties, unknown
at-rules, special functions) keep the quotes and escapes as written.
<===>
================================================================================
<===> custom_property/input.scss
a {
  --b: 'x';
  --c: 'a#{1 + 1}b';
  --d: 'it\'s';
  --e: "q'q";
}
<===> custom_property/output.css
a {
  --b: 'x';
  --c: 'a2b';
  --d: 'it\'s';
  --e: "q'q";
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> special_function/input.scss
a {
  b: type('x' "y");
  c: -a-calc('d');
}
<===> special_function/output.css
a {
  b: type('x' "y");
  c: -a-calc('d');
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> supports/input.scss
@supports (--a: 'b') {
  c {d: e}
}
<===> supports/output.css
@supports (--a: 'b') {
  c {
    d: e;
  }
}
<===>
================================================================================
<===> unknown_at_rule/input.scss
@foo 'bar' "baz";
<===> unknown_at_rule/output.css
@foo 'bar' "baz";
